  "body": "The following are listed in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#sandboxed-modals-flag : \r\n\r\n        window.alert()\r\n        window.confirm()\r\n        window.print()\r\n        window.prompt()\r\n        the beforeunload event\r\n\r\nWhen that sandbox flag was implemented in WebKit and Chromium, execCommand(\"print\") had to be handled too. I understand this is a non-standard feature and the status of https://w3c.github.io/editing/execCommand.html is not clear, but I'm opening this issue for the record.\r\n\r\nThis was a review feedback from @ayg  in https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/pull/6618",
